        "id": 1833664
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-04T17:59:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just a thought: should we allow authenticated messages with detached payloads?\n\nIt\u0027s not totally clear to me how we\u0027d specify it, but it seems like we should allow cases where the COSE_Sign1 payload value is `nil`. Else we may have backed ourselves into a corner if there are use-cases where the payload is very large.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 338,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 338,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "94fabed432cac28b1ed129487e194f7f3437ecca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "72f8eb94_13111f69",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/IRemotelyProvisionedComponent.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 338,
      "author": {
        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-04T21:03:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can do the types similarly to COSE_Sign1, i.e. `payload: bstr .cbor T / nil,`. `nil` indicating \"detached content\" and it would be down to the server endpoint to define how the payload is otherwise delivered or derived. Would that be adding `/ nil` be good enough?",
      "parentUuid": "8223955b_b9d6558e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 338,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 338,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "94fabed432cac28b1ed129487e194f7f3437ecca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "092da9c4_d9907c63",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/IRemotelyProvisionedComponent.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 338,
      "author": {
        "id": 1833664
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-04T21:08:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yup, I was thinking we\u0027d just use COSE_Sign1\u0027s nillable payload facility.\n\nWhat didn\u0027t occur to me, until you pointed out the obvious, is that we can just throw `/ nil` in the generic and I think it\u0027s good to go. In my mind I was concocting a more complicated multiple-parameter generic `AuthenticatedMessage` type.\n\nHaving a generic type parameter option with nil feels odd to me, but I think it\u0027s technically fine.",
      "parentUuid": "72f8eb94_13111f69",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 338,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 338,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "94fabed432cac28b1ed129487e194f7f3437ecca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
